    "id": "randomized-bit-model",
    "version": "1",
    "description": "3-SAT: given a CNF formula on n variables with m clauses, each clause an OR of at most three literals (variables or negated variables), decide whether some assignment satisfies every clause. Time counts bit operations (equivalently, steps of a multitape Turing machine or a word RAM with O(log(n+m))-bit words, up to (n+m)^{O(1)} factors) on the standard encoding of the formula. The algorithm may use independent uniform random bits; on every input it must halt on every run within the time bound and answer correctly with probability at least 2/3. Deterministic algorithms qualify. One algorithm for all n and m.",
    "definition_url": "https://github.com/openai/math/blob/7ef5c0cc5ca4b0e072b7a050fca09ab24bc6fa3a/preprints/The-Exponential-Time-Hypothesis-is-False-October-25-2026/paper.pdf"
  },
  "score": {
    "id": "subexponential-log-exponent",
    "version": "1",
    "symbol": "alpha",
    "definition": "Worst-case time (n+m)^{O(1)} 2^{n/(log n)^(alpha-o(1))} on every run: for every fixed epsilon>0, at most (n+m)^{O(1)} 2^{n/(log n)^(alpha-epsilon)} for all large n; per-input success probability at least 2/3.",
    "direction": "higher-is-better",
    "encoding": "rational-string",
    "minimum": "0",
    "maximum": "100"
  },
